== Trivia ==
* On December 6, every year, Isaac is reskinned as former Nintendo president [[wikipedia:Satoru Iwata|Satoru Iwata]] as tribute. December 6 was also Iwata's birthday. He has the same stats as Isaac, but starts with {{i|The Gamekid}} and {{t|Cartridge}}. {{i|How to Jump}} and {{i|Treasure Map}} are also more likely to appear.
* {{dlc+|r+}} Due to the special methods required to access them, runs ending on {{E|Mother}} and {{E|The Beast}} feature slightly unique mechanics:
** Runs ending on Mother will go through the alternate route as normal; the rooms leading to them are opened automatically. The trap doors leading to {{s|Mines}}/{{s|Ashpit}} I and {{s|Mausoleum}}/{{s|Gehenna}} I will not open until {{i|Knife Piece 1}} or {{i|Knife Piece 2}} has been obtained, respectively. Both items will be visible in [[Treasure Room]]s on the alternate route.
** In runs ending on the Beast, {{E|Mom}}'s boss room can be exited normally, making the marked skull optional. No trophy appears after defeating The Beast; the results screen will appear automatically.{{dlc-}}
*** Due to an oversight, if a [[Devil Room]] or [[Angel Room]] spawns after defeating Mom and the [[Boss Rush]] is open, leaving the special room can cause the Boss Rush entrance to attempt to appear on the same wall as the boss room door. If it does, Boss Rush will be inaccessible for that run.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r+}} In runs ending on {{E|Delirium}}, there are two guaranteed entrances to {{s|The Void}}:
** On {{s|???}} after defeating {{E|Hush}}.
** After defeating {{E|???}} in the {{s|Chest}}, or {{E|The Lamb}} in the {{s|Dark Room}}.
{{dlc-}}

